# MASTER PROJECT PROMPT — MODERN AQUARIUM E-COMMERCE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, 3D web developer, e-commerce architect, and QA engineer.

Build a complete, responsive, premium aquarium e-commerce website for a real client named **Modern Aquarium**.

Reference website: https://aquatic-e-commerce-store.vercel.app/

Use the reference only to understand the aquarium retail domain and shopping requirements. Create a distinct, original design with better usability, polished animations, clear navigation, and a complete WhatsApp ordering workflow.

Do not build just a landing-page mockup. Build a functioning, maintainable application with reusable components, structured product data, search, filters, cart management, product details, an admin area, and working order links.

## 1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVES

The website must:
- Sell ornamental freshwater fish, koi, and optionally marine fish.
- Sell aquariums, tanks, plants, substrates, decorations, equipment, food, and accessories.
- Sell ornamental birds and bird-care products.
- Offer aquarium setup, installation, maintenance, cleaning, aquascaping, and consultation services.
- Allow customers to order individual products or a complete cart through WhatsApp.
- Support product variants, quantities, prices, and stock availability.
- Mark birds as Store Pickup Only.
- Allow the shop owner to update products and prices through an admin interface.
- Work on mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop.
- Use free and open-source libraries and avoid mandatory paid services.

The primary conversion action is WhatsApp ordering, not online payment.

